invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_power keeps the digit a step reads in a local of its
  own frame, which nothing wipes, so the four low bits of the exponent
  are in that frame when the call returns. Every signature still comes
  out right. The runs that look for a value cannot find this one: they
  look for two words side by side, and four bits are in every byte of
  memory. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test also runs the exponentiation under dp
  and under dq and requires the two stacks it leaves to be the same
  (test/rsa_sign_equiv_differential.h), and the two keys' last digits
  differ.

--- old
        table_select(pick, &table, exponent_digit(e, i), k);
--- new
        volatile uint64_t digit = exponent_digit(e, i);
        table_select(pick, &table, digit, k);
